<title>FRANCE: FIMALAC LBCP PA SAYS IBCA/FITCH MERGER TALKS ONGOING.</title>
<headline>FIMALAC LBCP PA SAYS IBCA/FITCH MERGER TALKS ONGOING.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-08-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>French holding company Fimalac SA said on Monday that merger talks were still ongoing between its London unit credit rating agency IBCA Ltd and Fitch Investors Service LP of New York but that it was premature to talk about a final agreement.</p>
<p>&quot;I confirm that we are in discussions on the possibility of a merger,&quot; said Veronique Morali, managing director of Fimalac, who contacted Reuters to clarify the company's official position after an earlier report said the merger texts were all but signed.</p>
<p>Fitch's majority shareholder is the Van Kampen group of Grand Haven, Michigan.</p>
<p>Fimalac is a holding company with interests in industry, communications and market research.</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom +33 1 4221 5452</p>
